{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1481614-leviathan-the-tempest","id":1481614,"title":"Leviathan the tempest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-21T12:31:33-07:00","id":1481614,"title":"Leviathan the tempest","content":"It's what you think it is<br /> I would like to know what you think of this fangame<br /> Also how do you feel beast affects it's potential place in cofd? After all the makara familly is basically made to model sea monsters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T14:36:25-07:00","id":1481619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anyoneatall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1481614-leviathan-the-tempest#post1481614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what you think it is<br /> I would like to know what you think of this fangame<br /> Also how do you feel beast affects it's potential place in cofd? After all the makara familly is basically made to model sea monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Leviathan is more the splat of Cataclysms than the splat of Sea Monsters, that aspect isn't much of a problem.<br /> <br /> In one of the other threads, I mentioned how one of the problems with fangames is they'll try and tack on a gameline level approach to a monster that is, substantially, not enough to really support that approach. Leviathan is one such case. It's not the worst of the big four fangames, and by virtue of being one of those (and also not Genius, the general exception to the big four fangames) it's definitely more robust than many of it's peers and does a lot to fill out it's material more fully and coherently, but at the end of the day, it's definitely a case study of how the virtues of Chronicles that make it conducive to fangames is also it's biggest vice. I can't say it's 2nd Edition fills me with confidence.<br /> <br /> Anyways, on a broader, more meta-textual point of conversation, if threads like this is going to be a trend, why not a &quot;Let's Talk About Fangames!&quot; and just bring up whatever fangame you want to pick people's brains over at the time it comes up for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T14:58:48-07:00","id":1481621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1481614-leviathan-the-tempest?p=1481619#post1481619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, on a broader, more meta-textual point of conversation, if threads like this is going to be a trend, why not a &quot;Let's Talk About Fangames!&quot; and just bring up whatever fangame you want to pick people's brains over at the time it comes up for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>For reference, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1479656-about-fangames\">the thread the OP made on that very topic three weeks ago</a>.<br /> <br /> Having been on the RPGnet thread for the game's first edition circa 2012-ish, my takeaway was that it came away a little patchwork,* didn't really deliver on its at-the-time proposed &quot;Leviathan is the Paleozoic to Werewolf's Paleolithic&quot; vibe, wound up a lot fiddlier than it strictly needed to be (requiring more monstrous forms to use more powerful abilities is neat, but having more forms than werewolves get and needing to break down power intensity for each of those levels is a geometric expansion that Geist got rid of in its 2e for a reason), and ended up trying to bend the ChroD Size mechanics into a shape they weren't built for to facilitate kaiju movie action at a scale that doesn't work well with street-level personal/group stories. It had some neat stuff in there, and I'd say the vibe was that it was about 70-90% to being a fully realized project, but it still needed a bit of polish and trim.<br /> <br /> When last I looked, Leviathan 2e had five things listed in its Inspirations section, only one of which remotely resembles a story about sea monsters and two of which were just real geopolitical events from the mid-2010s; it created an Integrity trait that somehow managed to be more complicated than &quot;combination of Humanity, Harmony, and Clarity&quot; would imply; and still had a Hunter conspiracy with the ability to impose &quot;has a kill-sat pointed at you&quot; on player characters, weighted the same as the Hunted Condition. It did not fill me with confidence in its utility as a tabletop roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* There were people complaining at the time of Beast's KS that the Begotten were just Sin-Eaters with werewolves' metaphysical origins and a culture blending the Lancea et Sanctum and the Autumn Court. Leviathan's blend of concepts made those complaints read very entertainingly to me.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-21-2022, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T07:24:13-07:00","id":1481659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1481614-leviathan-the-tempest?p=1481619#post1481619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of the other threads, I mentioned how one of the problems with fangames is they'll try and tack on a gameline level approach to a monster that is, substantially, not enough to really support that approach. Leviathan is one such case. It's not the worst of the big four fangames, and by virtue of being one of those (and also not Genius, the general exception to the big four fangames) it's definitely more robust than many of it's peers and does a lot to fill out it's material more fully and coherently, but at the end of the day, it's definitely a case study of how the virtues of Chronicles that make it conducive to fangames is also it's biggest vice. I can't say it's 2nd Edition fills me with confidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO Promethean and Mummy both have the same problem, of being based on a monster that isn't broad enough to support a full gameline, and they're both official. Promethean has it worse - there's really only one story you <i>can</i> tell in Promethean, and while it's a good story it doesn't wear well with repetition.<br /> <br /> Leviathan, in fact, feels a lot like a poor man's Mummy. It's got most of the elements - monsters from an ancient origin, phenomenal cosmic powers that mostly you can't use because they're locked behind difficult prerequisites, cult management as a central gameplay element; but the systems are less polished, and the mythos and imagery less interesting, just as Genius mines the same inspirations as Mage, but not as well. (Also, the Hunter conspiracy is totally unneeded - Leviathans not only can, but should, fight each other for resources the way vampires do.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}